From: Emmanuel Velez Garcia <velezgarciaemmanuel25@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 16:49:35 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Validate inventory click slot bounds

The slot in PacketPlayInWindowClick is a signed short read straight off the
wire, and only the lower bound was checked. Several click modes in
Container#clickItem index the slot list with it unchecked, so a crafted
packet makes the handler throw IndexOutOfBoundsException on the main
thread. That is caught and logged with a full stack trace per packet, so
spamming it floods the log and the disk.

Rejects slots outside the open container in the packet handler, and adds
the same bound inside clickItem for callers that reach it another way.

diff --git a/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/Container.java b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/Container.java
index 486b940be465128462aeb1007c63165a4ef8e8f7..0278f21122dfc564b112279125ac5e9764c24dbf 100644
--- a/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/Container.java
+++ b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/Container.java
@@ -116,6 +116,14 @@ public abstract class Container {
     }
 
     public ItemStack clickItem(int i, int j, int k, EntityHuman entityhuman) {
+        // VoidSoulSpigot start - defence in depth against out of range slots.
+        // Several click modes below index the slot list with the raw slot number from
+        // the packet, some of them without even a lower bound. -1 and -999 are the
+        // "outside the window" markers and stay valid.
+        if (i != -1 && i != -999 && (i < 0 || i >= this.c.size())) {
+            return null;
+        }
+        // VoidSoulSpigot end
         ItemStack itemstack = null;
         PlayerInventory playerinventory = entityhuman.inventory;
         int l;
diff --git a/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/PlayerConnection.java b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/PlayerConnection.java
index f1a611889c487ee27a73798488c82699d2807883..e2bdac9a7050df45059c25442ceb320eb9f17ba1 100644
--- a/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/PlayerConnection.java
+++ b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/PlayerConnection.java
@@ -1498,6 +1498,15 @@ public class PlayerConnection implements PacketListenerPlayIn, IUpdatePlayerList
                     return;
                 }
 
+                // VoidSoulSpigot start - reject clicks on slots outside the open container.
+                // The slot is a signed short straight off the wire, and several click modes
+                // index the slot list with it unchecked, so a crafted packet can spam
+                // IndexOutOfBoundsException from the packet handler.
+                if (packetplayinwindowclick.b() >= this.player.activeContainer.c.size()) {
+                    return;
+                }
+                // VoidSoulSpigot end
+
                 InventoryView inventory = this.player.activeContainer.getBukkitView();
                 SlotType type = CraftInventoryView.getSlotType(inventory, packetplayinwindowclick.b());
 
